# Example 0119: Possibility Violation
# A possibly property that fails: from some state, no path reaches the condition
# Demonstrates: possibly, recoverability, counterexample note

---
deadlock_detection: false
---
# A document can be moved to the trash and restored, or purged from the
# trash for good. Every trashed document can still be restored, but once
# purged it can't come back, so "the document can always become active
# again" fails.
#
# The counterexample ends in a state where the possibly is false, and a note
# says the step after which no path reaches its condition.

action Init:
    status = "active"

atomic action Delete:
    require status == "active"
    status = "trash"

atomic action Restore:
    require status == "trash"
    status = "active"

atomic action Purge:
    require status == "trash"
    status = "purged"

# Holds: a trashed document can still be restored.
assertion Restorable:
    return always (status == "trash" implies possibly status == "active")

# Fails: after Purge, no path leads back to an active document.
assertion Recoverable:
    return always possibly status == "active"
